# This repository ships no Python packaging — no sdist, no wheel, no virtualenv, no test
# runner. What follows is only what this tree actually produces. It replaced GitHub's
# Python template, of which 78 of 89 rules could never have matched anything here.

### Python bytecode ###
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

### Tool caches ###
.ruff_cache/

### Pre-refactor archive, kept out of the tree ###
backup/

### Installed state, not source ###
# install.py symlinks the chosen theme bundle's wallpapers into ~/.config/qtile/, which is
# itself a symlink into this repository, so these land on tracked paths. Committing them
# pinned one theme's UUID into version control and made every theme switch dirty the tree.
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-dark.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-light.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-dark-highlight.png
configuration/qtile/wallpaper-light-highlight.png

### web-greeter generated artifacts ###
# Produced by helper/patch_web_greeter.py — should not be committed.
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/theme.css
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.png
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.jpg
configuration/web-greeter/themes/*/wallpaper.jpeg
# Per-theme copy of themes/_shared/ — only the canonical source under
# themes/_shared/ is tracked.
configuration/web-greeter/themes/[!_]*/_shared/
